A||||9||stsmithgt||When you think you've been screwed||||13||
Z||000000||stsmithgt||01-25-2001||04:47 PM||||--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>When you think you're getting screwed... Look again. I just picked up the collision report on the accident I was in and they are recommending to ticket me for failing to yeild to the other vehicle, which lawfully entered the intersection before the light turned red. <BR>?????????????????????<BR>If that car was in the intersection, I would have seen it. All cars were stopped when my light turned green and there wasn't any car unusally poking out into the intersection. I'm not blind. I know I would have seen him if he was in the intersection. He didn't come across until he was behind me out of my view. Half the cars that pull up to where he was, pull it up into the crosswalk just so they can see what's going on. I can't believe this. A guy gets to drive across a large intersection not watching where he's going, gets to plow me off the road and I get ticketed for it and he gets off scott free with no ticket.  I can't believe I'm getting so screwed.<BR> That guy simply ran a red light just like hundreds of other people do every day.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-25-2001||05:07 PM||||Sorry to here that you are having such a bad time of it. I hope you get everything going alright again in time for summer.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||01-25-2001||05:40 PM||||FIGHT IT! Refuse to pay the fine and go to court. If you can find a witness, take a sworn statement in front of a notary and submit it as evidence. If the officer didn't witness what happened, you have a good chance of having it thrown out of court. The worst that can happen is you'll be found guilty and have to pay the court fee in addition to your ticket fee. But, sounds like you have a good chance to beat it. Also, if the officer doesn't show up (and beleve me, this happens a lot), it'll be thrown out automatically.<P>Good luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000003||DRH||01-25-2001||06:02 PM||||From the pictures it looks like the kind of damage that would happen if both cars were moving in almost the same direction. <P>Which way was he traveling? For example; if you were traveling north, turning west... Was he going south turning west also (right turn)? If you had a green arrow sounds like he did a rolling stop right on red.<P><BR>You might want to talk to a lawyer... The ticket could be the least of your problems if they pin the blame on you.<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000004||stsmithgt||01-25-2001||06:09 PM||||Yeah.  This lady is 62 years old.  I don't think she know jack about street light sequencing or any other detail that would stand up in court.  She didn't seem like the type that would want to go to court either.  I think I disappointed to officer by being able to come up with my license and other information needed so he wouldn't take me to jail.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  I looked more at the report and I thinking, "Oh that was him!"  I did see him stop his car short of coming into the intersection.  I just didn't know that was the guy that plowed into me.  He looked like he made an uncomfortable stop due to the light turning yellow.  That's when I scanned the intersection.  He was stopped.  He should have never attempted to go.  I was done scanning and the light turned green and I was on my way.  Apparently so was he.  The report says he was in the intersection while the light was green.  That is totaly false.  I want a mean ass lawyer now.  I'm planning on digging into one of my investment plans to fight this.  I hate to do it, but I want to win.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever2||01-25-2001||09:15 PM||||Absolutely, definitely, positively fight it!<BR>And don't worry, this one should be all yours.<P>"Those aren't my shoes, and the gloves didn't fit" - O.J. Simpson, <I>The People vs. O.J. Simpson</I><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||6
